<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-25">25 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Triangle Shirtwaist Factory fire kills 146 in New York</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Fire swept through a garment factory near Washington Square, and locked doors trapped workers, mostly young immigrant women. The disaster led to new fire safety and labour laws.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-24">24 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Hiram Bingham reaches the Inca citadel of Machu Picchu</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Guided by local farmer Melchor Arteaga, Yale lecturer Hiram Bingham climbed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/machu-picchu">Machu Picchu</a>, already known to local families. His photographs made the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inca-empire">Inca</a> site world-famous.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/florence" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/florence.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/august-21">21 August</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The Mona Lisa is stolen from the Louvre</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Italian handyman Vincenzo Peruggia walked out of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louvre">Louvre</a> with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mona-lisa">Mona Lisa</a> under his smock. The theft made the painting world-famous; it was recovered in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence">Florence</a> in 1913.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence">Florence</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louvre">Louvre</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/xinhai-revolution" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/xinhai-revolution.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/october-10">10 October</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The Wuchang Uprising sparks the Chinese revolution</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Revolutionary soldiers mutinied at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wuchang">Wuchang</a>, beginning the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xinhai-revolution">Xinhai Revolution</a>. Within months the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qing-empire">Qing dynasty</a> abdicated, ending more than two thousand years of imperial rule in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/qing-empire">Qing Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xinhai-revolution">Xinhai Revolution</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wuchang">Wuchang</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/british-india" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/british-india.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-12">12 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">George V announces the move of India's capital to Delhi</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">At the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi-durbar">Delhi Durbar</a>, attended by hundreds of thousands, King-Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-v">George V</a> announced that the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-india">British India</a> would move from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kolkata">Calcutta</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-delhi">New Delhi</a> was inaugurated in 1931.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-india">British India</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-14">14 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Roald Amundsen's party reaches the South Pole</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Norwegian explorer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roald-amundsen">Roald Amundsen</a> and four companions became the first people to reach the South Pole. Robert Falcon Scott's British party arrived 34 days later to find the Norwegian tent and flag.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/jana-gana-mana" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jana-gana-mana.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-27">27 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Tagore's &quot;Jana Gana Mana&quot; is first sung in public in Calcutta</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rabindranath-tagore">Rabindranath Tagore</a>'s Bengali song &quot;Bharoto Bhagyo Bidhata&quot; was first sung publicly at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kolkata">Calcutta</a> Session of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-national-congress">Indian National Congress</a>. Its first stanza was adopted by the Constituent Assembly of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> as the national anthem on 24 January 1950.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/british-raj">British Raj</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jana-gana-mana">Jana Gana Mana</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rabindranath-tagore">Rabindranath Tagore</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-national-congress">Indian National Congress</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Crisis</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/agadir-crisis">Agadir Crisis</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Agadir Crisis, or Second Moroccan Crisis, began in July 1911 when Germany sent the gunboat Panther to the Moroccan port of Agadir in protest against the French occupation of Fez.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-daan" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-daan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty · Peace</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-daan">Treaty of Da'an</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Treaty of Da'an was an agreement concluded in 1911 at Da'an, north-west of Sanaa, between the Ottoman Empire and the Zaydi imam Yahya Hamid al-Din.</p></div></li></ol></section>
