<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/italian-empire"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Italian%20Empire.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Italian Empire</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Italo-Turkish War begins, bringing coastal Libya and the Dodecanese under Italian control</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/wadai-empire"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Wadai%20Empire.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Wadai Empire</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Sultan Dud Murra surrenders after years of resistance from the countryside</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-honduras"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Honduras.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Honduras</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Manuel Bonilla invades with mercenaries financed by Samuel Zemurray</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-china"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20China.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of China</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Wuchang Uprising on 10 October begins the Xinhai Revolution</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/british-raj"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/British%20Raj.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>British Raj</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">George V announces the move of the capital from Calcutta to Delhi</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-nri"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Nri.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Nri</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A British expedition forces the Eze Nri to renounce his ritual powers</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/government/aristocracy"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Aristocracy.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Aristocracy</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Parliament Act ends the House of Lords’ power to veto bills passed by the House of Commons</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/government/parliamentary-democracy"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Parliamentary%20democracy.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Parliamentary democracy</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Parliament Act ends the House of Lords’ absolute veto over bills passed by the House of Commons</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/principality-of-monaco"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Principality%20of%20Monaco.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Principality of Monaco</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Monégasque Revolution of 1910 forces the first constitution on the hitherto absolute princes.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/modernism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Modernism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Modernism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Cubism is shown to the public at the Salon des Indépendants, and Kandinsky paints what he later called the first abstract painting</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/popol-vuh"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Popol%20Vuh.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Popol Vuh</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Edward E. Ayer's donation of 17,000 pieces, Ximénez's manuscript among them, to the Newberry Library in Chicago is completed</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/machu-picchu"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Machu%20Picchu.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Machu Picchu</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Melchor Arteaga leads Hiram Bingham to the site, which Bingham brings to international attention</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/northern-rhodesia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Northern%20Rhodesia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Northern Rhodesia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The British South Africa Company merges Barotziland-North-Western Rhodesia and North-Eastern Rhodesia as Northern Rhodesia</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/ho-chi-minh"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Ho%20Chi%20Minh.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Ho Chi Minh</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Sails from Saigon as a kitchen helper on the French steamer Amiral de Latouche-Tréville</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/delhi"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Delhi.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Delhi</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The capital of British India is announced to be moving to Delhi</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/kolkata"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kolkata.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kolkata</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The capital of British India moves from Calcutta to New Delhi</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/mona-lisa"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Mona%20Lisa.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Mona Lisa</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Vincenzo Peruggia, a Louvre employee, stole the painting</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/marie-curie"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Marie%20Curie.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Marie Curie</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Fails by one or two votes to enter the French Academy of Sciences, and is awarded the Nobel Prize in Chemistry</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/persian-constitutional-revolution"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Persian%20Constitutional%20Revolution.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Persian Constitutional Revolution</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">In December the shah's cabinet, backed by 12,000 Russian troops, expels the deputies of the Second Majlis</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/hundred-days-reform"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Hundred%20Days'%20Reform.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Hundred Days' Reform</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Xinhai Revolution succeeds, a result to which the failure of the late Qing reforms contributed</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/religion/native-american-church"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Native%20American%20Church.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Native American Church</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Victor Griffin, known as the last chief of the Quapaw, helps incorporate the Native American Church under Oklahoma law</span></li></ul></section>
